researchers in China have designed a  carbon-based paper that folds walks and  even turns corners on its own the paper  is made from an ultra-thin carbon based  material called graphene oxide selected  areas of the paper contract when heated  with infrared light and swell back up  again when the light is turned off  depending on where the sensitive areas  are and when the light hits them the  paper strips can walk forward backward  and even turn down the road such  materials could prove valuable for  making sensors and artificial muscles  for robots  [Music]
 

